# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/

# Build output. These are what `make clean` removes: the cross-build tree, the
# .deb staging area, and a binary from a plain `go build` in the repository
# root. The leading slash anchors the binary names to the root, so a directory
# or package named after the app elsewhere in the tree is still tracked.
build/
dist/
/s3duck-tui
/s3duck-tui.exe

# Go tooling leftovers: `go test -c` writes <package>.test, and a coverage run
# writes its profile wherever it is pointed (cov/ is where the README's
# combined unit + integration + e2e recipe puts its counters).
*.test
coverage.out
/cov/

# What an interrupted download leaves beside its target to resume from: a
# hidden partial file and its record. Only here if a download directory (or
# a local pane) points inside the checkout.
*.s3duck-part
*.s3duck-resume

# macOS writes these into any directory it browses, and this project ships
# darwin builds.
.DS_Store
